id: pm-beads-y6cp
title: Explain invalid Beads dependencies with bounded row repair packets
description: "Overlap checked against beads validate, core relationship analytics, pm-graph analytics, and pm-csv provenance. This adds Beads JSONL row addresses and exact external identities plus revalidated edge-removal proposals. It does not replace core topology or CSV cell provenance."
type: Feature
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-28T19:31:55.419Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T20:07:16.578Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: "A cycle involving three of 10000 rows returns those rows and edges within declared input, work and output budgets; every emitted candidate revalidates; malformed and unresolved references remain explicit gaps; no title-based identity inference."
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-28T19:32:23.416Z",codex-agent,"Overlap: beads validate already reports invalid JSON, dangling blockers and cycle messages; pm-graph owns workspace analytics; pm-csv owns table provenance. Use core RelationshipGraph and analyzeRelationshipExecution over opaque row tokens to preserve case-sensitive external identities. Add a read-only repair packet, bounded candidate edge removals, explicit gaps and source-byte revision guards. No tracker writes, journals or role-based lifecycle decisions are added."
  "2026-10-28T19:47:49.245Z",codex-agent,"Implementation: typed read-only packet and preview APIs, canonical CLI plus alias, lazy public graph SDK loading, exact UTF-8 source revision guard, isolated row gaps, integer work/input/output ceilings, and bounded fully revalidated edge-removal candidates. Targeted numeric/alias/extreme-value corpora and 512 seeded graph operation sequences compare an independent transitive-closure model, preserve every untouched native field, replay older inputs and verify native state read back through the real SDK. Existing import/export/transfer/reconciliation/outgoing model suites remain in the unchanged CI full gate. Behavioral revert in a disposable non-git copy suppressed only the new cycle witness; the 10000-row regression failed (expected one cycle, got zero). New module measured 100% lines, branches and functions. Follow-up required for previously ignored blocks-only provider rows; repair keeps them explicit gaps."
  "2026-10-28T19:49:13.653Z",codex-agent,"Real-data validation: public unbraind/pm-beads main a5946b1dc8ab1f2d33b0c84c81e5eb34be3073b2, tracker tree c0e59199996b59f0f10cbbf51ac8758a9fb5589a. Frozen non-git public copy: 109 rows, 69941 UTF-8 JSONL bytes, 0 native blocker edges/cycles/gaps. Baseline including lazy SDK startup: 670.67 ms. Synthetic in-memory cycle only: 3 row witnesses, 3 cycle edges, 1 revalidated corrective edit, 2 core analyses, 1132 compact JSON bytes, 41.88 ms. No git executable; tracker byte fingerprint and SDK-read state unchanged. Reproduce with node test/public-repair-validation.ts. Related follow-up pm-beads-np1y tracks blocks-only representation semantics."
  "2026-10-28T19:57:05.870Z",codex-agent,"Final boundary review added a shared producer/consumer schema for saved candidates: exact keys, dense bounded edit arrays, finite safe integer coordinates, exact string identities, no accessor or serialization-hook authority, and canonical field ordering. UTF-8 decoding preserves BOM bytes for SDK/CLI revision agreement. Final focused command: npm run build && npm run build:test && npm run docstring && node --test --test-concurrency=2 --experimental-test-coverage --test-coverage-include=repair.ts test/repair.test.ts. Result: 9 passed, zero skipped; repair.ts measured 100% lines/branches/functions. Additional metadata/docstring/flag tests: 13 passed. Linked pm test runs use pm-context none with workspace-context snapshot; source workspace plus none is correctly refused by the host. Native health passes with no extensions; extension-enabled local health has pre-existing pm-github host-version skew (pinned 2026.10.24 versus global extension 2026.10.28). No dependency pins or existing history were changed."
  "2026-10-28T20:04:21.968Z",codex-agent,"Final malformed-row corpus also covers unsafe title/name values before invoking the existing validator. An object-valued title with a non-callable toString is retained as an isolated invalid_record gap alongside usable cycle witnesses. Existing validate/import coercion is tracked separately by pm-beads-4kw8; blocks-only semantics remain pm-beads-np1y. Final focused suite: 9 passed, zero skipped, 100% lines/branches/functions; the 10000-row cycle case completed in 2551.76 ms including preview. Final public-copy replay preserved the same 109 rows and 69941 bytes: baseline 865.49 ms, synthetic cycle 77.45 ms, 1132 compact packet bytes, one validated edit, unchanged frozen tracker and SDK-read state."
  "2026-10-28T20:07:12.490Z",codex-agent,"Final packed acceptance passed on all 5 paths (npm global, Bun global, project-local, npx, bunx), host 2026.10.28, same 55-file artifact, SHA-256 d1d327cf5b5a17c3ea3dc402358fcbe7f47b0e8a8ed26886ecd594f2deb15190; artifact bytes unchanged after all invocations. Reproduce with node test/packed-repair-acceptance.ts. Final public-copy measurement after all boundary changes: 109 rows, 69941 JSONL bytes, baseline 311.44 ms, synthetic three-row cycle 28.69 ms, 1132 compact packet bytes, three edges and one revalidated edit; tracker fingerprint and SDK-read state unchanged. Full npm and Bun release gates are delegated to the unchanged CI matrix; exact-head run URLs and counts will be included in the PR before handoff. Claim released for orchestrator review; items intentionally remain open."
